  faqs: [
    {
      question: 'What business processes can AI automation handle?',
      answer: "AI automation works best on repetitive work, heavy on text, where a person currently reads, decides and types the result into another system: triaging inboxes and support tickets, extracting data from invoices, forms and contracts, answering staff questions from policy documents, drafting routine correspondence, and moving information between systems such as your CRM, finance platform and document store. Steps that follow fixed rules are usually cheaper to automate with a plain workflow; an AI model earns its place where the input is unstructured or needs judgement. Decisions with high stakes should keep a human approval step.",
